    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nUpdates the repository’s developer tooling to stop managing Python via mise and instead rely on uv (with a `.python-version` pin) for Python execution and environments.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Remove Python from mise-managed tool versions and add `.python-version` for Python pinning.\n- Update `bin/python` to run Python via `uv run` with an explicit project root.\n- Adjust setup/doctor messaging and checks to reflect the new Python management approach.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 2 out of 5 changed files in this pull request and generated no comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `bin/setup` | Updates setup section labels/messages to reflect uv-managed Python. |\r\n| `bin/python` | Switches Python invocation from `mise exec … uv run python` to `uv run --project … python`. |\r\n| `bin/doctor` | Removes Python from the mise tool verification list. |\r\n| `.python-version` | Adds a pinned Python version for uv/pyenv-style consumers. |\r\n| `.mise.toml` | Removes the Python tool pin so mise no longer installs Python. |\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-unified-db/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
